  "id": "mood-induction",
  "term": "mood induction",
  "definition": "Mood induction is a research procedure used to shift participants into a targeted positive, negative, or neutral mood so scientists can study how mood influences psychological, cognitive, and bodily processes. It can use methods such as emotionally toned sentences, music, or autobiographical memory recall, and its effects may be brief.",
